IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ia71-types`

-- Immigration Act 1971 (UK) — GOAL 3: OFFENCES, PENALTIES AND TIME LIMITS
-- (ss 24, 24B, 28).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1971-77.txt.

§ `Goal 3 — offences`

DECLARE `Maximum term` IS ONE OF
    `months` HAS `number of months` IS A NUMBER
    `weeks` HAS `number of weeks` IS A NUMBER
    `not triable on indictment`

-- s 24(F1)(d): on indictment, (A1) five years; (B1)-(E1) four years; (E1A)
-- with (A1) six years; (E1A) with (B1), (D1) or (E1) five years. s 24(1) and
-- s 24B: summary only.
@ref ss 24(F1)(d), 24(1), 24B(3)
@export The maximum imprisonment on conviction on indictment for an offence under s 24 or s 24B of the Immigration Act 1971 (UK): five years for entering in breach of a deportation order; four years for entering without leave, overstaying, or arriving without entry clearance or an ETA; six or five years for endangering life on a journey by water (with an (A1) or another offence); the s 24(1) and s 24B offences are summary only. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence facts`  @desc The offence
GIVETH A `Maximum term`
`the maximum on indictment for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o's `offence`
    WHEN `entering in breach of a deportation order (A1)` THEN `months` 60
    WHEN `entering without leave (B1)` THEN `months` 48
    WHEN `overstaying (C1)` THEN `months` 48
    WHEN `arriving without entry clearance (D1)` THEN `months` 48
    WHEN `arriving without an ETA (E1)` THEN `months` 48
    WHEN `endangering life on a journey by water, with an (A1) offence (E1A)` THEN `months` 72
    WHEN `endangering life on a journey by water, with a (B1), (D1) or (E1) offence (E1A)` THEN `months` 60
    OTHERWISE `not triable on indictment`

-- s 24(F1)(a)-(c): summary, England and Wales the general limit (six months
-- for an offence before it applied, (G1)); Scotland 12 months; Northern
-- Ireland six months. s 24(1): six months. s 24B(3)-(4): England and Wales
-- 51 weeks (six months before s 281(5) CJA 2003); Scotland and NI six months.
@ref ss 24(F1)(a)-(c), (G1), 24(1), 24B(3)-(4)
@export The maximum imprisonment on summary conviction for an offence under s 24 or s 24B of the Immigration Act 1971 (UK), by jurisdiction: for the s 24(A1)-(E1A) offences, the general limit in England and Wales (six months for an offence before it applied), 12 months in Scotland, six months in Northern Ireland; six months for the s 24(1) offences; for illegal working, 51 weeks in England and Wales (six months before s 281(5) CJA 2003) and six months elsewhere. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence facts`  @desc The offence, the jurisdiction, the general limit and the transitional facts
GIVETH A `Maximum term`
`the maximum on summary conviction for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o's `offence`
    WHEN `failing to observe a condition of leave (1)(b)` THEN `months` 6
    WHEN `remaining beyond the time allowed by s 8(1) (1)(c)` THEN `months` 6
    WHEN `breaching an immigration bail condition (1)(h)` THEN `months` 6
    WHEN `illegal working (24B)` THEN
        CONSIDER o's `jurisdiction`
        WHEN `England and Wales` THEN
            IF o's `committed before s 281(5) CJA 2003 in force` THEN `months` 6 ELSE `weeks` 51
        OTHERWISE `months` 6
    OTHERWISE
        CONSIDER o's `jurisdiction`
        WHEN `England and Wales` THEN
            IF o's `committed before the general limit applied` THEN `months` 6 ELSE `months` (o's `the general limit in months`)
        WHEN `Scotland` THEN `months` 12
        WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN `months` 6

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

-- s 24(3): the extended time limit in s 28(1) applies to (A1), (B1), (D1),
-- (E1), (E1A) and (1)(c). s 28(1)(a): "within six months after the
-- commission of the offence, or if it is laid within three years after the
-- commission of the offence and not more than two months after the date
-- certified". (3A), s 28(1A)(a): (1)(h) — "within the period of six months
-- beginning with the date of the commission", or "within the period of three
-- months beginning with the date when the person is first arrested ... if
-- that period expires after the end of" the first.
@ref ss 24(3)-(3A), 28(1)(a), (1A)(a)
@export The last day on which an information may be laid in England and Wales on the extended time limits in s 28 of the Immigration Act 1971 (UK): for the offences in s 24(3), the later of six months after the offence and (within three years after it) two months after the certified evidence date; for breach of a bail condition, the later end of the six months beginning with the offence and the three months beginning with the first arrest. NOTHING for offences without an extended limit. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence facts`  @desc The offence, its date, and the certified evidence date or first arrest date
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the last day to lay an information for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o's `offence`
    WHEN `breaching an immigration bail condition (1)(h)` THEN
        JUST (CONSIDER o's `first arrested on`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN sixBeginning
              WHEN JUST a  THEN `the later of` sixBeginning (`the last day of the` 3 `months beginning with` a))
    WHEN `overstaying (C1)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `failing to observe a condition of leave (1)(b)` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `illegal working (24B)` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE
        JUST (CONSIDER o's `evidence certified on`
              WHEN NOTHING THEN sixAfter
              WHEN JUST e  THEN `the later of` sixAfter (`the earlier of` (`add months` committed 36) (`add months` e 2)))
    WHERE
        committed MEANS o's `committed on`
        sixAfter MEANS `add months` committed 6
        sixBeginning MEANS `the last day of the` 6 `months beginning with` committed
